            "review_title": "Review at Chi Em Quan",
            "review_text": "Alvin C\nDa'an, Taipei61 contributions\n1\nHidden Gem. Must Visit for Authentic Vietnamese Food\nOct 2019 • Friends\nThis restaurant will surprise and delight you. It serves excellent Vietnamese cuisine presented beautifully in a comfortable environment. \n\nI’ve been there twice and on both occasions the place was full of young professionals. Based on the interactions between guests and staff many seem to be regulars. \n\nThe owner is from northern Vietnam and focuses on creating tasty and healthy meals. with a focus on healthy ingredients. \n\nThe restaurant is hidden in a small alley off the Ho Con Ruy roundabout in District 3 within walking distance of the of these national palace and Saigon cathedral. \n\nThe interior is cozy and tastefully decorated. The staff are polite and the menus are easy to understand, even if you don’t understand Vietnamese. \n\nAnd for animal lovers they have a pet duck that waffles around the restaurant and might choose to snooze under your table! \n\nI highly recommend this restaurant. It could be a highlight of your Ho Chi Minh visit.\nRead more\nWritten October 25, 2019",
